[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station with natural flow regime. GENERAL: Velocity area station located in straight gravel-bedded reach. STATION HYDROMETRY: Informal concrete low-flow control installed in 1966 - good hydraulic performance. D/s gravel had a short-term impact on modularity. Peak flow ratings derived from current meter gaugings. Highest known gauging 1.8m, 55cumecs (about 0.75 QMED). Simple extrapolation of rating to calculate high flows. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11). FLOW REGIME: Natural catchment.
CATCHMENT,Silurian shales in upper catchment; Triassic sandstone aquifer in lower catchment. Land use: predominantly hill pasture with a third forestry. Minimal floodplains. No significant catchment changes known.
Qmed Suitability,Suitable for QMED estimation.
Pooling Suitability,Higher floods based on large extrapolation of rating above highest gauging. Out of bank flow, gravel extraction downstream and close proximity to confluence all contribute to increase uncertainty in the confidence of larger flood events.
[END]
